WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Stain the tip of a growing root,
and look at it under a microscope.

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.890
A few cells show dark, thick chromosomes.

3
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.820
Those cells were caught
in the middle of dividing.

4
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.190
But nothing on the slide is moving.

5
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.540
Every cell is fixed at one
instant, like a single photo.

6
00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:22.290
So how can counting the cells
on one still slide reveal time?

7
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.240
In this mission, you'll learn to name a
cell's stage from what its chromosomes

8
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.310
are doing.

9
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.010
Then you'll work out why some chromatids
look V-shaped as they move apart.

10
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:37.250
Your mission: find out how counting
the cells on one slide can reveal time.
